{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Hecke.PauliChannelBinding","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Hecke.PauliChannelBinding","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic"],"declarations":4,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Hecke.PauliChannelBinding.pauli_channel_unbound","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Hecke.PauliChannelBinding.pauli_channel_unbound","kind":"theorem","line":76,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Hecke/PauliChannelBinding.lean#L76-L85","doc":"**Pauli channel is unbound.** For positive substrate `q`, the antisymmetric\n(Pauli) channel value `-q⁻¹` fails the binding criterion `0 < f < 1` because\nit is negative. Hence identical-nucleon (p-p, n-n) bonds — forced by Pauli\nantisymmetry into this channel — do not contribute binding. This is the\ncategorical backbone of the chirality→complete-graph result: only the p-n\nbonds survive. (The `Z·N` pair count and the deuteron magnitude are NOT\nclaimed here — see the scope note in the file header.) ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Hecke.PauliChannelBinding.pauliEigenvalue_neg","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Hecke.PauliChannelBinding.pauliEigenvalue_neg","kind":"theorem","line":70,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Hecke/PauliChannelBinding.lean#L70-L74","doc":"For a positive substrate `q`, the Pauli channel value `-q⁻¹` is negative. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Hecke.PauliChannelBinding.pauliEigenvalue","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Hecke.PauliChannelBinding.pauliEigenvalue","kind":"def","line":66,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Hecke/PauliChannelBinding.lean#L66-L68","doc":"The antisymmetric (alternating / Pauli) channel eigenvalue of the Hecke\ngenerator `(σ - q)(σ + q⁻¹) = 0`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Hecke.PauliChannelBinding.Binds","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Hecke.PauliChannelBinding.Binds","kind":"def","line":61,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Hecke/PauliChannelBinding.lean#L61-L64","doc":"A bond contributes binding iff its channel value is a positive sub-unity\nsuppression `0 < f < 1` (the strict bound test of the 2026-06-20 chirality\naudit; a non-positive value is unbound). ","signatureChunk":0}]}